      "content": "thanks for the tip on Cousto. i've looked into some of that but it feels too \"new age\" and soft for what i'm seeing. i'm seeing actual physical deviations. like, if i play a specific cluster of frequencies around 432Hz but offset by a microtonal dissonance, the local electromagnetic field seems to fluctuate and the \"will\" of the people in the room just... bends. they become highly suggestible or completely paralyzed.\n\nif we treat human consciousness as a complex oscillating system, we could probably model it as a series of nested wave functions. if i provide you with the frequency sets that caused the strongest physical displacement in my studio, can you help me derive a mathematical constant for \"cognitive permeability\"? i want to find the exact point where a sound wave can bypass mental resistance entirely.",
